  "notes": "West leads the ♣Q which South wins. South's only possible losers are in the diamond suit. Unfortunately, there are 4 possible losers in that suit.\n\nIf South immediately draws trump, the defense might be in a position to take 4 diamond tricks if that suit breaks 4-2. South should delay drawing trump and play on diamonds at trick 2 with the aim of ruffing South's fourth diamond in dummy.\n\nThe defense might try to counter by leading spades, but the contract may still succeed. If the defender with the long diamonds has only 2 spades, he will have no trumps to play after winning the third diamond lead.\n\nIf it turns out that diamonds were 3-3 all along, South's long diamond will be high. There will be no need to ruff it in the dummy.",
  "commentary_paragraphs": [
